<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Swift on Daniel Tsang</title><link>https://demo.stack.jimmycai.com/tags/swift/</link><description>Recent content in Swift on Daniel Tsang</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 19 Dec 2025 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://demo.stack.jimmycai.com/tags/swift/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Native Mobile App Development Day 1 - Swift Basics</title><link>https://demo.stack.jimmycai.com/p/native-mobile-app-development-day-1-swift-basics/</link><pubDate>Fri, 19 Dec 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://demo.stack.jimmycai.com/p/native-mobile-app-development-day-1-swift-basics/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://demo.stack.jimmycai.com/swift.png" alt="Featured image of post Native Mobile App Development Day 1 - Swift Basics" /&gt;&lt;h2 id="what-is-swift-"&gt;What is Swift ?
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Swift is a compiled programming language for all Apple platform. It mainly use in Apple ecosystems: iOS, macOS, watchOS, tvOS (SwiftUI). It is a Multi-Paradigm Language thats support Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), Protocol-Oriented Programming (POP) and Functional Programming.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id="swift-basics"&gt;Swift Basics
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2 id="constant-and-variables"&gt;Constant and Variables
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Variable - You can change the value whenever you want.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Constant - You cannot change the values once they are set.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;hello&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;Hello&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Constant&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;world&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;World&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Variable&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="type"&gt;Type
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="type-safety"&gt;Type Safety
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Swift allow us create variables as strings and integers, but also other data types too.
Swift can figure out the type of the variable based on its value. You cannot change the type of the variable later on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Example :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;aloha&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;Aloha&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Since we already set the value of aloha = &amp;ldquo;Aloha&amp;rdquo; which is a string. So that we can&amp;rsquo;t write this :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aloha&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1234&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="type-annotation"&gt;Type Annotation
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Common Reasons that we need to use type annotation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to use different type from swift&amp;rsquo;s default&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You don&amp;rsquo;t want to assign a value now.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Swift can&amp;rsquo;t figure out which type should be use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The first of those will be happen when you fetch data from the internet. Swift would not know the type if its some custom data type.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The second situation is quite common. Here is the example :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;//If you don&amp;#39;t specify Double, it will be integer as default&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Double&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;18&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;When you don&amp;rsquo;t want to assign value to a variable when its declaration :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;noValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="string"&gt;String
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Swift&amp;rsquo;s standard strings is not support contain any line breaks. For example:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;No pain, No gain !&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="multi-line-strings"&gt;Multi-line strings
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Since stand string not support line breaks. Multiline strings that shines when you need to store a lots of text across as many lines as you want.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;lyrics&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Oh, the misery
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Everybody wants to be my enemy
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Spare the sympathy
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Everybody wants to be my enemy-y-y-y-y
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="string-interpolation"&gt;String interpolation
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;I most of the application, we use string to show data, messages to user. Most of the time, the message isn&amp;rsquo;t static string, because we want to so some relevant data to the user which is dynamic. So that Swift support String interpolation to combine static string with variable (dynamic).Here&amp;rsquo;s the example :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;Peter&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;greeting&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;Hello &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;\(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; !&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;//outputs : Hello Peter !&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>